  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Perspective Stripes\n\nRows of a two-part phrase in two colours slide sideways at different speeds over a tilted plane that scrolls away in depth, while the phrase itself fades up large in the middle.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A title over a moving wall of repeated text: a slogan, a call to action, a repeated claim.\n- A dynamic backdrop that needs the message to stay readable in front.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The message has to be read in the rows themselves: they are small and busy.\n- A calm or minimal layout.\n\nVariables:\n- line_1 (string): Line 1, default \"Create your\"\n- line_2 (string): Line 2, default \"own video\"\n- font_size (number, 20-240): Font size, default 64\n- color_1 (color): Line 1 color, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- color_2 (color): Line 2 color, default \"#2563eb\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#fafafa\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Perspective Stripes\n\n  Rows of a two-part phrase in two colours slide sideways at different speeds over a tilted plane that scrolls away in depth, while the phrase itself fades up large in the middle.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerPerspectiveStripes.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-perspective-stripes\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"line_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Line 1\", \"description\": \"First line of the phrase, also repeated in every other row.\", \"default\": \"Create your\"},\n    {\"id\": \"line_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Line 2\", \"description\": \"Second line of the phrase, also repeated in the other rows.\", \"default\": \"own video\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the centre phrase in pixels. Wide text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 64, \"min\": 20, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color_1\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Line 1 color\", \"description\": \"Color of the first line and its rows.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color_2\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Line 2 color\", \"description\": \"Color of the second line and its rows.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Perspective Stripes</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wps-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: #0a0a0a; }\n        .wps-plane { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; width: 200%; height: 150%; transform-style: preserve-3d; }\n        .wps-row { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.5625em; }\n        .wps-row span { margin-right: 1.667em; }\n        .wps-g { position: relative; text-align: center; line-height: 1.2; z-index: 2; }\n        .wps-l { font-weight: 800; text-shadow: 0 0 0.625em var(--bg, #fafafa), 0 0 0.3em var(--bg, #fafafa); white-space: pre; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-perspective-stripes\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wps-clip\" class=\"wps-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wps-plane\" class=\"wps-plane\"></div>\n          <div id=\"wps-g\" class=\"wps-g\"><div id=\"wps-l1\" class=\"wps-l\"></div><div id=\"wps-l2\" class=\"wps-l\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-perspective-stripes\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\");\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--bg\", str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\"));\n            \n            var lines = [str(vars.line_1, \"Create your\"), str(vars.line_2, \"own video\")];\n            var cols = [str(vars.color_1, \"#0a0a0a\"), str(vars.color_2, \"#2563eb\")];\n            var stage = el(\"wps-clip\"), plane = el(\"wps-plane\"), g = el(\"wps-g\");\n            var l1 = el(\"wps-l1\"), l2 = el(\"wps-l2\");\n            l1.textContent = lines[0]; l1.style.color = cols[0];\n            l2.textContent = lines[1]; l2.style.color = cols[1];\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 64, 20, 240);\n            function fit() {\n              g.style.fontSize = base + \"px\";\n              var w = Math.max(l1.offsetWidth, l2.offsetWidth, 1);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * 0.88 / w);\n              g.style.fontSize = Math.max(6, base * k) + \"px\";\n              // The stripes follow the frame height (64 px at 1080), not the title size.\n              plane.style.fontSize = (root.clientHeight / 1080 * 64) + \"px\";\n            }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n\n            var COUNT = 9, SH = 1.25;\n            var rowEls = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < COUNT; i++) {\n              var r = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              r.className = \"wps-row\";\n              r.style.height = SH / 0.5625 + \"em\";\n              var ph = i % 2;\n              for (var j = 0; j < 14; j++) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = lines[ph];\n                s.style.color = cols[ph];\n                r.appendChild(s);\n              }\n              plane.appendChild(r);\n              rowEls.push(r);\n            }\n            // remocn-scenes: rows scroll 3 px a frame at 64 px type (stripe height 80 px), each row slides\n            // sideways at 2-4 px a frame, depth sets a faint opacity; plane = perspective 800 px, rotateX 45, rotateZ -15.\n            function draw(t) {\n              var U = 64, SP = COUNT * SH * 2;\n              var off = t * 3 / U;\n              plane.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) perspective(12.5em) rotateX(45deg) rotateZ(-15deg)\";\n              rowEls.forEach(function (r, i) {\n                var baseY = i * SH * 2 - off;\n                var wrapped = ((baseY % SP) + SP) % SP;\n                var y = wrapped - SH * 2;\n                var xs = (2 + (i % 3)) / U;\n                var xo = ((t * xs + i * 100 / U) % (2000 / U)) - 1000 / U;\n                r.style.top = (y / 0.5625) + \"em\";\n                r.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (xo / 0.5625) + \"em)\";\n                r.style.opacity = ip(wrapped, 0, COUNT * SH, 0.06, 0.3);\n              });\n              l1.style.opacity = ip(t, 20, 40, 0, 1);\n              l2.style.opacity = ip(t, 30, 50, 0, 1);\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
